<% texl.import "~/lib/stilo/index.texl" ~> (lib -> bind "stilo" lib.data.stilo) %>
<!--{ bd01 : markdown }-->
# Basis of design

Mezzanine floor beam — document MZ-002, revision B. The design data of the
[design report](beam-check.texl): codes, structure, materials, loads,
combinations and acceptance criteria. The
[calculation note](analysis.texl) imports them from here.
<% texl.import("../../library/steel.texl") ~> (lib -> bind "steel" lib.data) %>
<!--{ bd02 : rich }-->
## 1 Codes and standards

- EN 1990: Basis of structural design.
- EN 1991-1-1: Actions on structures — densities, self-weight, imposed loads
  for buildings.
- EN 1993-1-1: Design of steel structures — general rules and rules for
  buildings.

The recommended values of the Eurocodes are used. Consequence class CC2,
design working life 50 years.
<!--[ Marco: confirm the partial factors against the National Annex before issue. ]-->
<!--{ bd03 : markdown }-->
## 2 Structure

![A simply supported beam under a uniform load](figures/beam.svg)

<%
L = 6,                          # span in m
spacing = 2,                    # beam spacing in m
beams = 12,                     # number of beams of the gallery
section = steel.IPE.IPE300      # section proposed by the preliminary design
%>
The <% beams %> beams carry a gallery floor of composite steel deck and
screed. Each beam spans L = <% L %> m between two columns and carries a strip
of floor <% spacing %> m wide. It is simply supported: the end plate connections
transfer shear only. The deck is fixed to the top flange at every rib, so the
compression flange is restrained laterally and lateral-torsional buckling
does not occur. The preliminary design proposes an <% section.name %>.
<!--[ Anna: span and spacing from the client's brief, rev. B. ]-->
<!--{ bd04 : markdown }-->
## 3 Materials

<%
fy = steel.grade.fy,
E = steel.E,
gammaM0 = steel.gammaM0
%>
| Property | Symbol | Value |
|---|---|---:|
| Steel grade | | <% steel.grade.name %> |
| Yield strength | $f_y$ | <% fy %> N/mm² |
| Modulus of elasticity | $E$ | <% E %> N/mm² |
| Partial factor for resistance | $\gamma_{M0}$ | <% gammaM0 %> |
<caption>Table 1: Steel properties, from the steel library.</caption>
<!--{ bd05 : markdown }-->
## 4 Loads

Characteristic loads on the floor (EN 1991-1-1). The gallery is open to the
public, category C3, areas without obstacles for moving people. The
self-weight of the beam is added in the calculation, for each section
checked.
<!--{ bd06 : data }-->
<% loads: stilo.dataframe {
    columns: ["Load", "Type", "Area load (kN/m²)", "Line load (kN/m)"],
    rows: [
        ["Composite deck and screed", "permanent", 1.6, 1.6 * spacing],
        ["Finishes, ceiling, services", "permanent", 0.5, 0.5 * spacing],
        ["Imposed, category C3", "variable", 5, 5 * spacing]
    ]
} %>
<!--{ bd07 : markdown }-->
<%
line = loads.column "Line load (kN/m)",
gk = line 0 + line 1,      # permanent line load in kN/m, without self-weight
qk = line 2                # variable line load in kN/m
%>
On one beam: permanent load g<sub>k</sub> = <% gk %> kN/m and variable load
q<sub>k</sub> = <% qk %> kN/m.
<!--[ Anna: loads from the client's brief, rev. B. ]-->
<!--{ bd08 : markdown }-->
## 5 Load combinations

Partial factors of EN 1990, Annex A1, table A1.2(B), equation 6.10, for the
ultimate limit state (ULS); the characteristic combination, equation 6.14b,
for the serviceability limit state (SLS).
<!--{ bd09 : data }-->
<% combinations: stilo.dataframe {
    columns: ["Combination", "γG", "γQ"],
    rows: [
        ["ULS, fundamental", 1.35, 1.5],
        ["SLS, characteristic", 1, 1]
    ]
} %>
<!--{ bd10 : markdown }-->
<%
gammaG = (combinations.row 0) 1,
gammaQ = (combinations.row 0) 2
%>
The strength checks use γ<sub>G</sub> = <% gammaG %> and
γ<sub>Q</sub> = <% gammaQ %>; the deflection checks use the characteristic
loads.
<!--[ Marco: partial factors from EN 1990, table A1.2(B). ]-->
<!--{ bd11 : markdown }-->
## 6 Acceptance criteria

<%
deflection_total = 250,      # limit of the total deflection: L / 250
deflection_variable = 300    # limit of the deflection under variable load: L / 300
%>
| Check | Criterion |
|---|---|
| Bending, shear (ULS) | utilisation ≤ 1.0 |
| Total deflection (SLS) | δ ≤ L / <% deflection_total %> |
| Deflection under variable load (SLS) | δ<sub>q</sub> ≤ L / <% deflection_variable %> |
<caption>Table 2: Acceptance criteria.</caption>
